From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Video Player

Add the CromIKO player. Videos on web pages, also in frames of other
sites (where most streaming sites put their player), get a small round
button with the CromIKO mascot; playing audio gets one in the corner.
A tap opens the video full screen in the CromIKO player, without the
site's controls, overlays and ads: the player keeps the site's media
element, so streams only the site can play keep playing, and hides
everything else. While it is open, taps go to the player only, so the
site cannot open pop-ups on them. "CromIKO player" in the app menu
opens the main video of the page.

Tap controls:
- tap: show or hide the controls (the first tap goes full screen)
- double tap left or right: 10 s back or forward; more taps add more
- double tap in the middle: play or pause
- hold: 2x speed while holding
- swipe sideways: seek; swipe up or down: brightness (left) or
  volume (right)
- pinch: zoom to fill the screen or fit the video

Buttons: play/pause, 10 s back/forward, time bar with buffered part,
playback speed (0.25x to 3x), subtitles, picture in picture (where the
platform has it), lock the controls, fit/zoom/stretch, rotate, close.
More options: loop, background play (undoes the pause sites make when
the app goes to the background) and a sleep timer. The player offers
to continue where you stopped, and audio gets a page with the mascot.
A long press on the small button hides the buttons on that page.

The page script (res/raw/cromiko_video.js) runs in every frame through
the CromikoPageScripts bridge, which gets executeInAllFrames.

